<title>GERMANY: Bayer details 1996 results.</title>
<headline>Bayer details 1996 results.</headline>
<dateline>LEVERKUSEN, Germany 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996 (in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group sales				  48,608  vs 44,580</p>
<p>    Group capital expenditure		3,777   vs 3,169</p>
<p>    Group workforce (end of year)	  142,200 vs 142,900</p>
<p>    Group personnel costs		    15,096  vs 14,624</p>
<p>    Group research and technology costs  3,608   vs 3,259</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     4,464   vs 4,185</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   2,747   vs 2,421</p>
<p>    Group operating profit		   4,510   vs 4,111</p>
<p>    Group net interest income (expense)  (87)    vs 11</p>
<p>    Gp non operating result (expense)    (46)    vs 74</p>
<p>    Parent net profit			  1,361   vs 1,158</p>
<p>    Parent pre-tax profit		    2,097   vs 1,898</p>
<p>    Parent sales				 18,187  vs 18,029</p>
<p>    Dividend				     1.70    vs 1.50 marks</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of German chemical and drugs group is Bayer AG. Analysts had expected pre-tax profit to rise by an average 8.2 percent with estimates ranging between 4.36 billion and 4.7 billion marks. Sales were seen climbing an average 7.6 percent to anywhere between 47 billion and 48.68 billion marks. The dividend was expected to climb 10 pfennigs to 1.60 marks. Some of the numbers had already been released last week after the group's supervisory board meeting.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
